<title>USA: CUC International Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>CUC International Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended April 30,	  1997		    1996</p>
<p>REVENUES</p>
<p>    Membership and service fees   $544,037	     $455,006</p>
<p>    Software				80,634		 60,473</p>
<p>   Total Revenues			624,671		515,479</p>
<p>EXPENSES</p>
<p>    Operating			    209,539		158,327</p>
<p>    Marketing			    219,793		205,202</p>
<p>    General and administrative	86,360		 70,066</p>
<p>    Interest income, net	     (8,689)		(2,240)</p>
<p>Interest expense, 3% convertible</p>
<p>     notes				  3,634</p>
<p>   Total Expenses			510,637		431,355</p>
<p> INCOME BEFORE INCOME TAXES	  114,034		 84,124</p>
<p>  Provision for income taxes	  43,561		 32,003</p>
<p> NET INCOME				 70,473		 52,121</p>
<p> Net Income Per Common Share(a)	 0.17		   0.13</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of Common</p>
<p>and Dilutive Common Equivalent</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding		   434,006		396,665</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Net income per share for 1997 quarter computed based upon &quot;if-converted&quot; method which excludes interest expense attributable to three percent convertible subordinated notes issued February 11, 1997 and includes the 14,966,004 weighted average shares (17,959,205 actual issued shares) in the total weighted average number of shares outstanding that would be issued if the notes were converted.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
